    "chunk_text": "\u0d85\u0d82\u0d82\u0d9a \u0d85\u0d82\u0d82\u0d9a 2446/282446/28 \u2013 \u2013 20252025 \u0da2\u0dd6\u0dbd\u0dd2 \u0db8\u0dc3 \u0da2\u0dd6\u0dbd\u0dd2 \u0db8\u0dc3 2121 \u0dc0\u0dd0\u0dd0\u0db1\u0dd2 \u0dc3\u0db3\u0dd4\u0daf\u0dcf\u0dcf \u0dc0\u0dd0\u0dd0\u0db1\u0dd2 \u0dc3\u0db3\u0dd4\u0daf\u0dcf\u0dcf \u2013 \u2013 2025.07.212025.07.21No. 2446/28 \u2013No. 2446/28 \u2013 MONDAY, JULY 21, 2025 MONDAY, JULY 21, 2025\n\n(Published by Authority)(Published by Authority)\n\nPART I: SECTION (I) \u2013 GENERALPART I: SECTION (I) \u2013 GENERAL\n\nGovernment NotificationsGovernment Notifications\n\nappoint Mr. Piyal Darshana Guruge, Attorney-at-low, No.04, Richard De Soysa Housing Scheme, Koswatta, Battaramulla. to be the arbitrator and refer the aforesaid dispute to him for settlement by arbitration.\n\nDr. Anil Jayantha Fernando, Minister of Labour.\n\nColombo.11th July, 2025.\n\nMy No.: IR/COM/01/2023/25.\n\nTHE INDUSTRIAL DISPUTES ACT, CHAPTER 131 OF THE LEGISLATIVE ENACTMENTS OF CEYLON(1956 REVISED EDITION)\n\nMr. S. R. T. P. Sinhabahu, No. 71/2, Nape, Nelundeniya.\n\nand\n\nNational Aquatic Resources Research & Development Agency, Crow Island, Mattakkuliya, Colombo 15.\n\nSTATEMENT OF MATTER IN DISPUTE\n\nThe matter in dispute between the aforesaid parties is \u2013\n\nWhether Mr. S. R. T. P. Sinhabahu, employed as the cartographer of National Aquatic Resources Research & Development Agency had been caused injustice by not being placed in the salary Category A R 1-2, in which officers of parallel grades have been placed in the adsorption into posts from 01.07.2008 under Management Services circular 30 and if such injustice had been caused, to what relief he is entitled.\n\nH. M. D. N. K. Wataliyadda, Commissioner General of Labour.\n\nDated at the Office of the Commissioner General of Labour,Colombo, on this 30th day of June, 2025.\n\nEOG 07 \u2013 0245_____________________\n\nMy No.: IR/COM/02/2024/02.\n\nTHE INDUSTRIAL DISPUTES ACT, CHAPTER 131 OF THE LEGISLATIVE ENACTMENTS OF CEYLON(1956 REVISED EDITION)\n\nOrder under Section 4(1)\n\nWHEREAS an Industrial Dispute in respect of the matter specified in the statement of the Commissioner General of Labour which accompanies this order exists between,\n\nMrs. G. H. N. Shyamali, No. 573/9, Mahakatuwana Road, Homagama.\n\nand"
